  "statement": "The expression \\(\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\) denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(x\\). Find the value of\n\n\\[\\left\\lfloor\\frac{2002!}{2001!+2000!+1999!+\\cdots+1!}\\right\\rfloor .\\]",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2002-p33.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "2000 We break up 2002! \\(=2002(2001)\\) ! as\n\n\\[\\begin{gathered}\n2000(2001!)+2 \\cdot 2001(2000!)=2000(2001!)+2000(2000!)+2002 \\cdot 2000(1999!) \\\\\n>2000(2001!+2000!+1999!+\\cdots+1!)\n\\end{gathered}\\]\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n\\[2001(2001!+2000!+\\cdots+1!)>2001(2001!+2000!)=2001(2001!)+2001!=2002!\\]\n\nThus we have \\(2000<2002!/(2001!+\\cdots+1!)<2001\\), so the answer is 2000 .",
